      "side": 1,
      "message": "This name is a bit misleading because this value is one-past the maximum address that the MMU allows the CPU to access (through TTBR0), which is likely to cover normal memory, device memory, and (mostly) invalid addresses; in particular, it isn\u0027t the \"end\" of the (normal) memory region, which \"`MEM_END`\" might imply.\n\nGiven how infrequently this constant will be used, WDYT of giving it a longer, more explicit name such as `ADDRESSABLE_LIMIT` or `MAX_VIRT_ADDR`?",
